  "Area": "Unclassified",
  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "John is walking east at a speed of \\(3\\) miles per hour, while Bob is also walking east, but at a speed of \\(5\\) miles per hour. If Bob is now \\(1\\) mile west of John, how many minutes will it take for Bob to catch up to John?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(30\\)",
    "B": "\\(50\\)",
    "C": "\\(60\\)",
    "D": "\\(90\\)",
    "E": "\\(120\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Bob starts behind John, and both walk east. Bob therefore gains on John at a rate of\n\\[\n5-3=2\\text{ miles per hour}.\n\\]\nAt that rate, closing the \\(1\\)-mile gap takes\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ hour}=30\\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\nThus Bob catches John after \\(30\\) minutes, choice A.",
